---

## 0. One-paragraph answer

Upstream's orchestration plane and this repository's are **opposite by default and structurally different in
kind**. Upstream is **keyword-gated doctrine over a programmatic run engine**: nothing exists until the user
writes a `mass ulw` spelling, at which point a hidden pointer tells the model to read `mass-ulw/SKILL.md`,
which mandates a planning reference, a one-run-per-phase DAG on the native `workflow` tool, a node prompt
contract, a goal binding and a verification wave. This repository has the *inverse* posture — **mechanical
default-on**: every qualifying session auto-provisions the staged "MPD Default" team on its first step
(`lib/session-start.js:229-269`, enabled by `packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml:218-224`) — plus a
**stronger** quality-gate plane and a Web approval plane that upstream does not have at all. The headline gap
is therefore D1 (opposite defaults, which is exactly the stated "agent-teams 不再默认" requirement); the
headline structural gap is D3 (the two `workflow` tools share a name but not a contract). The most important
non-obvious finding: **the plugin's own schema already defaults `sessionTeamPolicy.mode` to `off`
(`lib/index.js:91-98`) — only the bundle row turns it on**, so de-defaulting is a one-row config decision, not
a code change.

