## 2. Upstream semantics (what `mass ulw` / the workflow plane actually is)

### 2.1 Activation is keyword-gated, and the pointer is deliberately conditional
`omo-senpi` ships one `skill-pointers` component holding a uniform keyword table. The mass group is
`MASS_ALIAS = (?:mass[\s-]*ulw|ulw[\s-]*mass|mulw|meth)` over the user's input with quoted/relayed regions
blanked; a match injects a hidden (`display:false`) custom message pointing at `mass-ulw/SKILL.md`.
`packages/omo-senpi/AGENTS.md` states the doctrine explicitly: *"A keyword proves a mention, not a request, so
the pointer text is conditional (...) rather than asserting intent"*, and overlapping mentions all fire
(`mass ulw-loop` injects both mass-ulw and ulw-loop). Sources:
[skill-pointers/index.ts](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/src/components/skill-pointers/index.ts),
[omo-senpi/AGENTS.md](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/AGENTS.md),
[onboarding/SKILL.md](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/skills/onboarding/SKILL.md)
("Mass-ulw: `mass ulw` opens dependency-ordered multi-agent DAG orchestration").

### 2.2 The skill contract
[mass-ulw/SKILL.md](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/skills/mass-ulw/SKILL.md)
frontmatter: *"Drives dependency-ordered child work through the native workflow tool, one run per phase with
retry/amend/send recovery."* Body: use it when the user asks for mass-ulw, a DAG, staged fan-out, or work with
real dependencies; *"A run covers ONE phase's dependency-ordered lanes and NEVER a whole multi-phase job"*;
under `ulw-loop`/`ulw-execute` the loop owns the goal, this skill owns only the phase's run.
"Goal before start": every run is goal-bound (`create_goal`), and *"node and run completion claims are false
until proven against captured evidence"* — the change that made this explicit upstream is
[PR #7175](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/7175) ("bind mass-ulw runs to a goal carrying
result verification").

### 2.3 The planning reference is mandatory
[references/planning.md](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/skills/mass-ulw/references/planning.md)
self-describes as *"Mandatory planning reference (...) read in full BEFORE defining any graph"*: decomposition
by component / file domain / phase (collect -> verify -> synthesize), *"Default shape is fan-out, then
fan-in"*, and the sharp rule *"A 2-node graph with no dependency between the nodes is not a dag - use plain
parallel `task` spawns instead."*

### 2.4 The node prompt contract, linted (advisory only)
[dag-lint.ts](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/src/components/task/dag-lint.ts)
checks `prompt` for `TASK:` and `STOP WHEN` and pushes warnings naming
`TASK/DELIVERABLE/SCOPE/VERIFY/STOP WHEN`; the file's own header says warnings *"never reject"*.

### 2.5 The execution surface is a programmatic run engine
*"Build and run every dag INSIDE an eval cell. The eval kernel installs the `tool.workflow` proxy and the
extension publishes a small JS SDK at `OMO_DAG_SDK_ROOT`"* — see
[dag-sdk-root-provisioning.ts](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/src/extension/dag-sdk-root-provisioning.ts)
and [plugin/runtime/dag/sdk.js](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/plugin/runtime/dag/sdk.js)
("Every call funnels through `globalThis.tool.workflow({ action, ... })`"). The SDK profile is
`dag.define/node/start`, `run_id` + snapshot lifecycle, and a stored definition library (`OMO_DAG_LIBRARY`).

### 2.6 Team vs dag is an explicit routing doctrine
`ulw-research` (both copies) routes by trigger: a plain research request goes to the **team path** (critique and
expand loops are team mechanics), while `mass ulw research` goes to the **dag path at mass scale** — "attack is
conversation, and dag nodes do not talk". See
[ulw-research/SKILL.md](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/skills/ulw-research/SKILL.md)
and [changes.md](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/blob/dev/packages/omo-senpi/changes.md).

### 2.7 There is no session-start team policy upstream
Nothing in the inspected upstream components provisions a team at session start. The whole plane is armed by
the user's text.

