## 5. Candidate options (no decision taken here)

* **C1 — flip the default off (config-only).** Edit the bundle row (`cordis.patch.yml:218-224`), the legacy
  installer row (`scripts/install-profile.mjs:177`), the preset startup text (`presets/mpd/agent.cordis.yml:80-86`)
  and the documented rule (`packages/mpd-bundle/README.md:22-42`); rewrite the assertions in
  `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/session-start-team.mjs:85,87,129,133` and `scripts/install-profile.mjs:261-262` to pin
  the NEW posture. Zero plugin-code risk (the schema already defaults off). Closes D1, D8.
* **C2 — complexity-gated provisioning.** Keep auto mode but add a qualification predicate over the first turn
  in `lib/session-start.js` (+ schema value in `lib/index.js:91-98`). Closes D1, D8, D9. Risk: a heuristic is
  not mechanically provable and duplicates the preset's own sizing doctrine.
* **C3 — OMO-style keyword pointer component.** A new prompt-input component with one keyword table injecting a
  hidden conditional pointer; no auto-provisioning. Closes D2, D1. Any shipped skill target drags in a
  `skills/**` change + VENDOR_LOCK re-pin (single-writer rule).
* **C4 — adapt mass-ulw doctrine onto the DSH workflow tool.** Doctrine only (skills/**): one run per phase,
  fan-out/fan-in, node contract, explicit verification node, `create_goal` binding, plus an explicit statement
  of the DSH tool's real limits. Closes D3, D4, D7, D9, D10, D12. Must NOT copy upstream verbs that do not
  exist here.
* **C5 — structural parity inside the adopted plugin.** (a) advisory create-time lint for work tasks /
  degenerate graphs, (b) STOP-WHEN-equivalent contract field, (c) goal binding for team delivery. Closes D5,
  D6, D7, D4. Highest risk: each edit is an mpd-delta region + registry regeneration + mount proof.

Hard constraints for any option: the `/agent-teams` manual entry stays byte-identical in behaviour; the Web
approval plane and the quality gate must not regress; adopted-plugin edits must be delta regions with a clean
`--check` and a regenerated context-pair registry; any `skills/**` change rides the same commit as its
VENDOR_LOCK re-pin.

